{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 496 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2e55508d366bdbec92bc1f8bac74183134cdb03e342127a1e83a55918f029a5c" :edb/db-before-t 495 :edb/db-after-t 496 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533808 50 #inst "2026-10-05T02:15:27.271Z" 13194139533808 true] [17592186105828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252722 13194139533808 true] [17592186105828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252729 13194139533808 true] [17592186105828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252733 13194139533808 true] [17592186105828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252736 13194139533808 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252715 13194139533808 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252739 13194139533808 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252759 13194139533808 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252763 13194139533808 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252770 13194139533808 true] [17592186105830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252742 13194139533808 true] [17592186105830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252745 13194139533808 true] [17592186105830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252777 13194139533808 true] [17592186105830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252784 13194139533808 true] [17592186105830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252798 13194139533808 true] [17592186105831 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252749 13194139533808 true] [17592186105831 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252753 13194139533808 true] [17592186105831 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252756 13194139533808 true] [17592186105831 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252791 13194139533808 true] [17592186106010 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533808 true] [17592186106010 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=3, \\\\ b & =AC=7, \\\\ m∠A & ={128}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{128}^{∘}=0.788\\,010,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{128}^{∘} \\\\  & =10.5\\cdot (0.788\\,010) \\\\  & ≈8.27,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." 13194139533808 true] [17592186106013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533808 true] [17592186106013 1145 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =168\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =139.278… \\\\  & ≈139{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =139-90 \\\\  & =49{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252715 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252716 13194139533808 true] [17592186252715 1089 "q-161107" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252715 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252715 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/ef8379b21526455a723369fda4360e2d7d3ef3cf54ce7d7767df7bd160a169f4.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $5\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252715 1113 #uuid "f87bfa18-cb4b-532f-a120-eb1fc8ba9d73" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252715 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}\\,b}{4} \\\\ \\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}} & =\\frac{\\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}}\\,b}{4} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{b}{4} \\\\ b & =4\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=4\\,\\text{cm}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252717 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252718 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252719 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252720 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252721 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252717 13194139533808 true] [17592186252716 1110 #uuid "d5461aee-52b1-557e-bf04-fc2749454404" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252717 1034 "4\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252717 1111 #uuid "71051edb-3799-546b-bb07-b4109d22063d" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252718 1034 "5\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252718 1111 #uuid "84f0e954-89a2-5293-a2d2-7afdd09b3167" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252719 1034 "4.5\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252719 1111 #uuid "66327986-35d6-58fb-a241-38d01113ee5b" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252720 1034 "3\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252720 1111 #uuid "70bf0e37-e344-590f-8a78-4ab9085dd44c" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252721 1034 "5.5\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252721 1111 #uuid "5e5cad3b-9c6d-5123-bc8d-6a8a0fc29a2b" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252722 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252723 13194139533808 true] [17592186252722 1089 "q-18027" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252722 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533808 true] [17592186252722 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f11e50891625fb39de472762aaaff23edf43372e37fcdf55d129da1125c0ff8a.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252722 1113 #uuid "dce972d1-c315-563b-b53d-1667a53ac8c6" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252722 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=26, \\\\ b & =AC=22, \\\\ m∠A & ={11}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘}=0.190\\,809,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 22\\cdot 26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘} \\\\  & =286\\cdot (0.190\\,809) \\\\  & ≈54.57,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252724 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252725 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252726 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252727 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252728 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252725 13194139533808 true] [17592186252723 1110 #uuid "412bec09-9848-55da-83f4-8e76ea17a7d4" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252724 1034 "49.76" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252724 1111 #uuid "022f82c7-77b4-567a-bdf7-87c9d11d9462" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252725 1034 "54.57" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252725 1111 #uuid "ed06fee6-9b9b-5d7f-85bc-51d8883fa1a7" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252726 1034 "51.12" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252726 1111 #uuid "7f41ac99-6bac-590a-a5e4-d71d4d19b31e" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252727 1034 "59.59" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252727 1111 #uuid "7529cde6-d376-5a48-b697-2e633a2be6f4" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252728 1034 "62.75" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252728 1111 #uuid "52d4290c-535d-56b5-b6a5-5e33583d1cb0" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252729 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252730 13194139533808 true] [17592186252729 1089 "q-279752" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252729 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533808 true] [17592186252729 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f41ad0635fb7bb426a387f825097a31dddb591861012f2543336a142832df9db.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ above is{{field-1}}." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252729 1113 #uuid "63f35d69-f7b6-5350-bda1-58836456b5aa" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252729 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=4, \\\\ a & =BC=8, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}=0.642\\,788,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.642\\,788) \\\\  & ≈10.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252731 13194139533808 true] [17592186252730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252732 13194139533808 true] [17592186252730 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252730 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252730 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252731 13194139533808 true] [17592186252730 1110 #uuid "11f94e53-0b67-542e-ab28-05b559fefcb4" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252731 1034 "10.3" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252731 1111 #uuid "6e8b0230-c390-5fcf-ae5b-94286b8c3243" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252732 1034 "16" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252732 1111 #uuid "95db3c31-3680-5524-ad5a-f20a09252d6f" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252733 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252734 13194139533808 true] [17592186252733 1089 "q-279753" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252733 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533808 true] [17592186252733 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/68977537a5f180dd483534ed1415326251d4a76a3dd0833e9701487cd8b5b33d.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252733 1113 #uuid "bdf0daac-77bb-5aff-b5b4-b17585570165" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252733 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=18, \\\\ b & =AC=12, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot (0.866\\,025…) \\\\  & ≈93.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252735 13194139533808 true] [17592186252734 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252734 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252734 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252735 13194139533808 true] [17592186252734 1110 #uuid "17a8e155-9b4b-5c2f-a86b-8f003fc3d07b" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252735 1034 "93.5" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252735 1111 #uuid "a18332e9-ae54-51b7-9174-c91fd57b832a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252736 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252737 13194139533808 true] [17592186252736 1089 "q-280260" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252736 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533808 true] [17592186252736 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/200dcd87827ae9683ba0ecb3b284509b31d32f9e0dc1b9736a260d2f7d71b0a0.png)\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252736 1113 #uuid "43d3023f-7620-56f7-b1e5-34278ad10bf8" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252736 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5, \\\\ a & =BC=5, \\\\ m∠B & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =12.5\\cdot (0.866\\,025) \\\\  & ≈10.83,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to **two decimal places**." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252738 13194139533808 true] [17592186252737 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252737 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252737 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252738 13194139533808 true] [17592186252737 1110 #uuid "f205d0ec-fd0c-56b2-b7dd-730d38e2c86a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252738 1034 "10.83" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252738 1111 #uuid "64dd2d6f-4132-5325-a17c-2604c9205784" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252739 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252740 13194139533808 true] [17592186252739 1089 "q-280279" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252739 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252739 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/866f869f43e2663c2f63a485049f84ae059e2fdcb73db0445eb355491957c66a.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Then,  $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252739 1113 #uuid "4cd24f26-3da7-5768-8fda-4ef54a05927a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252739 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =5b\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 25\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} & =5b\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\ 5b & =25 \\\\ b & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{ cm}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252741 13194139533808 true] [17592186252740 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252740 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252740 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252741 13194139533808 true] [17592186252740 1110 #uuid "e9abe5e8-19c8-51cc-9b14-025c933a9cec" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252741 1034 "5" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252741 1111 #uuid "72ba36bb-85d1-5d7e-9547-5965892086b7" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252742 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252743 13194139533808 true] [17592186252742 1089 "q-285703" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252742 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252742 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/dafaf2421aaa9be80c472b4dde7c941defb94f7f3533fda4ebb2fdcee2b60e31.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252742 1113 #uuid "10670437-a53f-54a7-827c-60721e1dcb8d" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252742 1145 "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/cd9363a3cc686ae45f49c982f4b31ad75b7c7897dcf7e8af58e530dba6946e1d.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈19.096\\,0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9+19.096\\,0 \\\\  & ≈35.182\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $35.2.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252744 13194139533808 true] [17592186252743 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252743 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252743 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252744 13194139533808 true] [17592186252743 1110 #uuid "60225b26-4beb-5112-95d4-575b266647ef" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252744 1034 "35.2" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252744 1111 #uuid "7f1bbc69-4932-5617-add9-177028e0de9a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252745 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252746 13194139533808 true] [17592186252745 1089 "q-285737" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252745 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252745 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/48dec69962b09e9c189de23c398db63066b6da8d62a04f1cd01fdc9f333f899f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533808 true] [17592186252745 1113 #uuid "46b5c7ca-430e-5b3c-a8d2-98242978c6b9" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252745 1145 "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/d6a654d3154ba8af8fc4f7654e62c6bacfede7017322aeed21a143e2634dcd14.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈13.856,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 13.856 \\\\  & =27.712.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $28.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252747 13194139533808 true] [17592186252746 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252748 13194139533808 true] [17592186252746 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252746 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252746 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252747 13194139533808 true] [17592186252746 1110 #uuid "bc3064e5-65a9-52da-8035-e036d1cf8bd0" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252747 1034 "28" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252747 1111 #uuid "1935d4a8-305b-510b-9fb0-b54f40302e9a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252748 1034 "32" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252748 1111 #uuid "b85c281b-eb20-5c69-86bf-088cc87f6ad6" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252749 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252750 13194139533808 true] [17592186252749 1089 "q-285754" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533808 true] [17592186252749 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/d6923f5883ea770ce243eb23594740461a689c01f63de0421bc6f5d73a39531d.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $7{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252749 1113 #uuid "9e31458f-9551-5d17-b2e2-ecd0b59352ec" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252749 1145 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =9.899… \\\\  & ≈10{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =10-7 \\\\  & =3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252751 13194139533808 true] [17592186252750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252752 13194139533808 true] [17592186252750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252750 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252752 13194139533808 true] [17592186252750 1110 #uuid "3f04898b-c111-5240-a51b-df999ec7ac96" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252751 1034 "10" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252751 1111 #uuid "8a421f88-0cc3-554d-a3d4-a5f12467ac28" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252752 1034 "3" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252752 1111 #uuid "99bdbd48-80eb-507e-8db0-5373f000be69" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252753 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252754 13194139533808 true] [17592186252753 1089 "q-285769" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252753 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533808 true] [17592186252753 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/33aff6da54b72146f89bbd580a889a4050bff89bca86ddb6b74b80f62875a470.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $5{\\text{ km}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252753 1113 #uuid "a0277ac5-084d-5f95-96ad-7aaf91ad51d1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252753 1145 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2.5\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =6.682… \\\\  & ≈7{\\text{ km}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n