{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252757 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252758 13194139533808 true] [17592186252757 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533808 true] [17592186252757 1041 "field-1" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252757 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252758 13194139533808 true] [17592186252757 1110 #uuid "5f34847c-430d-5b9a-9efe-461d37acca16" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252758 1034 "3" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252758 1111 #uuid "da6a522a-c94a-5f87-8fe6-dec13c346034" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252759 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252760 13194139533808 true] [17592186252759 1089 "q-365424" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252759 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252759 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/7ead42d83a971733b601f45dcc1ad545a52298fc8a800ba69344651a54f4830d.png)\n\nThe area of the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $20\\sqrt{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252759 1113 #uuid "910bcc12-cda3-52d7-97f0-5d0df60f458d" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252759 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=10\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{20\\sqrt{2}}{40} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252761 13194139533808 true] [17592186252760 1000 #e