ot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252765 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252766 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252767 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252768 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252769 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252767 13194139533808 true] [17592186252764 1110 #uuid "1f42efba-3c43-5af3-b94b-2a896d82a916" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252765 1034 "{60}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252765 1111 #uuid "b0a8743c-2e77-5dac-b6af-5ac66163c949" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252766 1034 "{40}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252766 1111 #uuid "e9f2fef2-658f-5118-a1db-a4a119a929d5" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252767 1034 "{45}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252767 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252767 1111 #uuid "c34abd96-d115-5a06-9fc3-2022aac0fa11" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252768 1034 "{30}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252768 1111 #uuid "a763dde3-26bc-5597-bedc-2e4887b49df2" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252769 1034 "{50}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252769 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252769 1111 #uuid "578ebb5d-42d4-589b-b6f3-160c20921ddf" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252770 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252771 13194139533808 true] [17592186252770 1089 "q-43339" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252770 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252770 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252770 1113 #uuid "572e5141-81e2-5943-a49c-616b72e60fae" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252770 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252772 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252773 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252774 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252775 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252776 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252776 13194139533808 true] [17592186252771 1110 #uuid "322587b7-fe86-53d9-be57-f73876c0b587" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252772 1034 "{35}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252772 1111 #uuid "2897c8db-de63-55c1-a7d3-d6ea16befdac" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252773 1034 "{25}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252773 1111 #uuid "425c24b3-9100-5c4a-9d0f-239708c57b2a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252774 1034 "{40}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252774 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252774 1111 #uuid "603861cb-e9a3-5001-8918-e43efcf15714" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252775 1034 "{45}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252775 1111 #uuid "f91d36b2-dee6-5f10-ac05-a8756725b8a9" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252776 1034 "{30}^{∘}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252776 1111 #uuid "7e445c5e-60be-5868-9a84-9f983f751955" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252777 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252778 13194139533808 true] [17592186252777 1089 "q-54339" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252777 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252777 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f1ae263b71fa17fd648464c24b307c064c9e657c2c9f6b36faf8c9819f1fb285.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252777 1113 #uuid "fe1c85ee-47ba-593d-bacd-c936fe57a2d9" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252777 1145 "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/a60b049aef53aef28802b084b3e445fd6253978500ca981d3b799977523cdd71.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.383,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 16.383 \\\\  & =32.766.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $33.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252779 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252780 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252781 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252782 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252783 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252781 13194139533808 true] [17592186252778 1110 #uuid "8fdb0015-4dcd-587c-bd43-3b48ddf3e176" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252779 1034 "38" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252779 1111 #uuid "d7732a51-13c3-5363-acc3-b3fe64d4d9a6" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252780 1034 "40" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252780 1111 #uuid "637d6825-dc45-557b-9a44-d8fde4cd6d9d" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252781 1034 "33" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252781 1111 #uuid "b2f05137-8fc5-57f8-98f6-6d2dc90d096a" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252782 1034 "42" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252782 1111 #uuid "466666bc-c2f6-516d-b952-5b01d307c035" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252783 1034 "30" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252783 1111 #uuid "faafefac-9945-5856-8c2c-d790b7b3a45e" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252784 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252785 13194139533808 true] [17592186252784 1089 "q-67787" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252784 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533808 true] [17592186252784 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/488389632139d269e24958275ee20a9e5f8582fd0966e4d935487d238a463180.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252784 1113 #uuid "447571ef-da3a-581f-92b7-e3d7f25719b2" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252784 1145 "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/68f5708d49577befe9bac6a7aaf6a54fcdb30dcd344367d2c69b8924093dbb61.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 14\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =84\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈56.315\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =17.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.994\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =56.315\\,8+16.994\\,8 \\\\  & =73.310\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $73.3.$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252786 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252787 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252788 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252789 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252790 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252787 13194139533808 true] [17592186252785 1110 #uuid "200c4f49-c890-5824-b8eb-2e8e52a478bb" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252786 1034 "76.6" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252786 1111 #uuid "b580489e-e94f-5cbc-b27b-3c297fe21961" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252787 1034 "73.3" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252787 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252787 1111 #uuid "c9621403-78d9-5d37-84ca-a887fc46ee3f" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252788 1034 "88.2" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252788 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252788 1111 #uuid "a4e9d9ae-24b5-5e1d-8b09-4ed642753ca2" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252789 1034 "69.8" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252789 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252789 1111 #uuid "27505146-5134-5a54-ba92-c0c40afea1ad" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252790 1034 "83.4" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252790 1111 #uuid "f5994c2f-d174-50cc-96ab-4b312b0397c2" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252791 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252792 13194139533808 true] [17592186252791 1089 "q-72764" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252791 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533808 true] [17592186252791 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f53996727138b9442ac041cf492618db8287b54ba652c4f9e375cdde27dc1862.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252791 1113 #uuid "ddae1abe-3b8a-5a4b-93fb-4640928027e8" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252791 1145 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =67.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =53.190… \\\\  & ≈53{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =53-34 \\\\  & =19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252793 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252794 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252795 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252796 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252797 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1041 "selection" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252793 13194139533808 true] [17592186252792 1110 #uuid "60ef8113-28b4-5f71-8864-c30d1be347e7" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252793 1034 "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252793 1111 #uuid "02407f4c-bc2f-57d4-a03a-816ca5fbeb3d" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252794 1034 "23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252794 1111 #uuid "f4159129-2fc8-59d3-b09a-df1f80b72530" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252795 1034 "25{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252795 1111 #uuid "5c9ecca0-5e66-5ce5-9c26-73ed7084cedd" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252796 1034 "13{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252796 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252796 1111 #uuid "e0060577-42ec-5a97-b005-2452c4097dd8" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252797 1034 "34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533808 true] [17592186252797 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533808 true] [17592186252797 1111 #uuid "7707ed10-f84f-5306-9010-02fcf8332461" 13194139533